    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. List All Files in Google Drive Folder for RAG Ingestion\nRetrieves a list of all files within a specified Google Drive folder so they can later be processed, chunked, embedded, and ingested into a RAG pipeline.\n\n**Input**:\n-Google Drive Folder Name: the name of the folder containing sales documents.\n\nFetches all file metadata, including `version`, `name` and `id`, which ensures always keeping the latest version of each file in the vector database.\n\n**Output**:\n-A list of files with metadata including file ID, name, and version.\n",
        "height": 608,
        "width": 384,
        "color": 5
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        400,
        -448
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "b368c128-69c3-4b6d-84cb-3756447b936e",
      "name": "Sticky Note4"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2. Loop Through Files and Trigger RAG Ingestion Subflow\nIterates over each file returned from the Google Drive folder and invokes a dedicated subflow that handles RAG ingestion for a single file, ensuring efficient memory usage and stable performance.\n\n**Input**:\n-The array of files, including metadata from the previous node (`id`, `name`, `version`).\n\nProcesses files sequentially, passing one file at a time into the subflow to avoid loading multiple documents into memory simultaneously.\n\n**Output**:\n-For each file: a successful trigger of the RAG ingestion subflow with the file metadata passed as input.\n-On failure: the loop stops for the current file, logs the error, and continues with the next file to prevent blocking the entire ingestion run.\n",
        "height": 656,
        "width": 576,
        "color": 5
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        800,
        -496
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "f5ba4257-a488-402b-9687-7ed8e284e349",
      "name": "Sticky Note5"
    },
